" That is rung 5, parental permission. Voting against it shows he opposes rung 5. It doesn't show which of rungs 1–4 he holds, so I coded both of its passages `direction-only`.\n- **AB 963 (2021-2022) and AB 510 (2023-2024):** these are the parents' bills of rights, and Wirch voted No on both. Each lists 15 or more separate parental rights, and only one of them covers names and pronouns. I coded them `multi-subject`, and under the vote ladder a No on a bill like that proves nothing about one clause.\n\nI coded all six record passages `in-term` because they are his own Senate votes. The term dates given were \"unknown\", so this rests on the votes being cast in the Senate, not on a known term.\n\n**Needs source:** Wirch's own words on AB 103, or on whether schools should tell parents about a student's name or gender-identity change. Without that, no rung can be seated.","ttft_ms":16166,"type":"result","duration_ms":39658,"uuid":"82dff39d-1752-4fe8-9373-df908000b687","ttft_stream_ms":1342,"time_to_request_ms":78,"first_content_frame_ms":1342,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
